        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: New York Islanders, New York Rangers, Pittsburgh Penguins, New Jersey Devils, New York Knicks, New York Liberty\n- Places: New York metropolitan area, Madison Square Garden, Israel\n- Events: 1974–75 NHL playoffs\n- Topics: NHL franchises, sports venue tenancy, news coverage\n\nFacts:\n- In the 1974–75 NHL playoffs, the New York Islanders defeated the New York Rangers in three games in the first round.\n- In the 1974–75 NHL playoffs, the New York Islanders then defeated the Pittsburgh Penguins in seven games in the Quarter-finals after losing the first three games.\n- The New York Rangers are one of three NHL franchises in the New York metropolitan area, along with the New Jersey Devils and New York Islanders.\n- Madison Square Garden is the home venue of the New York Rangers of the NHL, the New York Knicks of the NBA, and, since 1997, the New York Liberty of the WNBA.\n- Vos Iz Neias? primarily covers the New York metropolitan area and Israel.",
